 ## Background
-The method originates from work on splatting errors and antialiasing, specifically the "Splat Tenderer" approach [S1, unofficial]. It was used to render volumes such as a hollow tube checkerboard and terrain datasets, demonstrating antialiasing benefits through splatting [S1, unofficial]. The Data Subsetting variant was developed for batch rendering of 3D isosurface figures using X13 on CPU-only clusters, addressing the need to reduce large HPC NetCDF files for plotting [S2, unofficial].
+The method originates from work on splatting errors and antialiasing, specifically the "Splat Tenderer" approach [S1, unofficial]. It was used to render volumes such as a hollow tube checkerboard and terrain datasets, demonstrating antialiasing benefits through splatting [S1, unofficial]. The Data Subsetting variant was developed to reduce large HPC NetCDF files for plotting, and is used to prepare data for X12 and X13 plotting scripts on laptop or CPU-only clusters [S2, unofficial].
 
